.TH WORMINAL 1 worminal\-VERSION
.SH NAME
worminal \- simple terminal based on st
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B worminal
.RB [ --master
.IR user@host ]
.RB [ \-aiv ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR class ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR font ]
.RB [ \-g
.IR geometry ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR iofile ]
.RB [ \-T
.IR title ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR title ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR line ]
.RB [ \-w
.IR windowid ]
.RB [[ \-e ]
.IR command
.RI [ arguments ...]]
.PP
.B worminal
.RB [ \-aiv ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR class ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR font ]
.RB [ \-g
.IR geometry ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR iofile ]
.RB [ \-T
.IR title ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR title ]
.RB [ \-w
.IR windowid ]
.RB \-l
.IR line
.RI [ stty_args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B worminal
is a simple terminal emulator.
Each launch opens a window and tab in the local per-user workspace service.
The service owns the PTYs and ordered tabs and persists after all windows close.
Use
.B worminald --stop
to stop it and end its tabs.
.B --master user@host
connects over SSH to a service on that host; the remote account needs
.B worminald
in its PATH. Further hosts can be reached with ordinary SSH inside a tab.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
disable alternate screens in terminal
.TP
.BI \-c " class"
defines the window class (default Worminal).
.TP
.BI \-f " font"
defines the
.I font
to use when worminal is run.
.TP
.BI \-g " geometry"
defines the X11 geometry string.
The form is [=][<cols>{xX}<rows>][{+-}<xoffset>{+-}<yoffset>]. See
.BR XParseGeometry (3)
for further details.
.TP
.B \-i
fixes the window size.
.TP
.BI \-n " name"
defines the window instance name (default worminal).
.TP
.BI \-o " iofile"
writes all the I/O to
.I iofile.
This feature is useful when recording worminal sessions. A value of "-" means
standard output.
.TP
.BI \-T " title"
defines the window title (default 'Worminal').
.TP
.BI \-t " title"
defines the window title (default 'Worminal').
.TP
.BI \-w " windowid"
embeds worminal within the window identified by
.I windowid
.TP
.BI \-l " line"
use a tty
.I line
instead of a pseudo terminal.
.I line
should be a (pseudo-)serial device (e.g. /dev/ttyS0 on Linux for serial port
0).
When this flag is given
remaining arguments are used as flags for
.BR stty(1).
By default worminal initializes the serial line to 8 bits, no parity, 1 stop bit
and a 38400 baud rate. The speed is set by appending it as last argument
(e.g. 'worminal -l /dev/ttyS0 115200'). Arguments before the last one are
.BR stty(1)
flags. If you want to set odd parity on 115200 baud use for example 'worminal -l
/dev/ttyS0 parenb parodd 115200'. Set the number of bits by using for
example 'worminal -l /dev/ttyS0 cs7 115200'. See
.BR stty(1)
for more arguments and cases.
.TP
.B \-v
prints version information to stderr, then exits.
.TP
.BI \-e " command " [ " arguments " "... ]"
worminal executes
.I command
instead of the shell.  If this is used it
.B must be the last option
on the command line, as in xterm / rxvt.
This option is only intended for compatibility,
and all the remaining arguments are used as a command
even without it.
.SH SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Break
Send a break in the serial line.
Break key is obtained in PC keyboards
pressing at the same time control and pause.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Print Screen
Toggle if worminal should print to the
.I iofile.
.TP
.B Shift-Print Screen
Print the full screen to the
.I iofile.
.TP
.B Print Screen
Print the selection to the
.I iofile.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-Page Up
Increase font size.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-Page Down
Decrease font size.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-Home
Reset to default font size.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-y
Paste from primary selection (middle mouse button).
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-c
Copy the selected text to the clipboard selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Shift-v
Paste from the clipboard selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl-t
Create and select a tab.
.TP
.B Ctrl-w
Close the selected tab in all windows.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Tab, Ctrl-Shift-Tab
Cycle tabs in the current window.
.TP
.B Ctrl-1 through Ctrl-8, Ctrl-9
Select a tab by position, or the last tab with Ctrl-9.
.TP
.B Alt-1 through Alt-9, Alt-0
Select the exact tab slot (Alt-0 selects slot 10). An empty slot does nothing.
.TP
.B Ctrl-n
Open a new window and tab.
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
.B worminal
can be customized by creating a custom config.h and (re)compiling the source
code. This keeps it fast, secure and simple.
